 | 0948 | `ntdll`: on PS5, a synchronous write of 4 KiB or less to a regular file (no event, APC, write-through or unbuffered I/O) is kept and written with the ones after it at the same handle's next position, in one `pwrite` of up to 64 KiB; any other use of a file (`server_get_unix_fd`, a name opened or looked at, `NtClose`, `NtDuplicateObject`, the process's end) writes them first. The console's kernel takes about a millisecond a write: Aggelos 2 saved its config 4 bytes at a time on every menu picture |
 | 0949 | `mmdevapi`: on PS5, the audio driver's `PKEY_AudioEndpoint_PhysicalSpeakers` replaces the one kept in the registry each time the devices are listed. mmdevapi kept the first it stored, so a prefix that once ran in stereo told DirectSound games stereo after a game's Sound output in PC5 was set to 5.1 or 7.1 (`WINE_PS5_SPEAKERS`). A driver without an answer leaves what is kept |
 | 0951 | `kernelbase`: `SetConsoleTitleW` succeeds without doing anything for a console program started without a console window (`CONSOLE_HANDLE_SHELL_NO_WINDOW`), as the title starts every game. It failed with `ERROR_INVALID_ACCESS`, and .NET's `Console.Title` threw `System.IO.IOException` before Streets of Rage 4 started; on Windows the program would have had a window to take the title |
+| 0952 | `vkd3d-shader`: `saturate()` in a vertex shader before vs_3_0, which has no saturate modifier, is `min(max(x, 0), 1)`, as native fxc writes it. It was `mov_sat`, which Far Cry's own d3dx9 assembler refused when it assembled the listing of the shader for the sun's glow again ("invalid instruction modifiers") |
 | 0953 | `wow64`: a 32-bit caller's allocation with its own address requirements (an alignment) and no highest address is kept below the 32-bit process's limit, as on Windows; it landed above 4 GiB and the game faulted on the address's low half. From PS5_MihawkOS |
 | 0954 | `server`: on PS5, an opened file's directory is resolved with `realpath` once and kept (64 entries, checked by device and inode), so an open costs two system calls instead of one a path component. From PS5_MihawkOS (its 2080) |
 | 0955 | `ntdll`: on PS5, the directories a process resolved are kept by their upper-cased Windows path (1024 slots) and a lookup starts from the longest one, checked with one `fstatat`; a directory's case sensitivity is not asked (the console's disk is). From PS5_MihawkOS (its 2081) |
